CSES Europe was established in June 2018 in Dublin as a directly-owned subsidiary of the Centre for Strategy & Evaluation Services LLP to continue performing assignments for the EU institutions and other EU-based clients post-Brexit. CSES LLP was in turn established in 1999 by former senior members of Ernst & Young&rsquo;s economics and management consulting practice. 
CSES Europe specialises in the following types of work:
&middot; Evaluations of policies, programmes and legislation 
&middot; Impact assessments; 
&middot; Policy, organisation and strategic reviews; 
&middot; Specific studies, e.g. studies relating to SMEs, specific sectors (e.g. space ,chemicals, electronics and chips, tourism) entrepreneurship, access to finance, industrial policy, competitiveness, the internal market, regional development, justice and home affairs.
